# Cold email pipeline — installed via `crontab -e`.
#
# nightly_agent.sh (3 AM) does the real work now: research, free Apollo
# contact search, write, critique, and send up to 20 emails per night, all
# done by a live Claude Code session (see NIGHTLY_RUNBOOK.md), fully
# autonomous, no dashboard approval step. This replaces the old
# run_pipeline.sh (qwen3:8b) + hourly send_approved.sh combo for that flow
# — don't run both, they'd race over the same companies.
#
# send_approved.sh stays as a safety net for anything left sitting at
# status='approved' that the nightly run didn't send for some reason.
# reply_tracker.sh is unrelated and unaffected, keep as is.
0 3 * * * /Users/harshsharma/Desktop/Work_Dir/cold_email/scripts/nightly_agent.sh
0 * * * * /Users/harshsharma/Desktop/Work_Dir/cold_email/scripts/send_approved.sh
0 8 * * * /Users/harshsharma/Desktop/Work_Dir/cold_email/scripts/reply_tracker.sh
